            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0352" n="264" xml:id="pg264"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.51/1752: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-11-30T18:00:00-05:00">November 30, 1933—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. Our 97, November 27 [<hi rendition="#italic">26</hi>], noon.<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d224-f1"/> Despite repeated efforts Dawson has been unable to see
                    Olaya, but his private secretary told Dawson that the President would sign the
                    debt bill before tomorrow evening. President would, however, point out at the
                    same time the advisability of Congress in its next session amending the act in
                    certain particulars.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
